<title>AUSTRIA: OMV to finish Libya oil pipeline by end 96.</title>
<headline>OMV to finish Libya oil pipeline by end 96.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian oil and chemicals group OMV AG said on Tuesday it would complete work on a 370 km pipeline to pump crude from the Murzuk oilfield in Libya by the end of this year.</p>
<p>OMV chief executive Richard Schenz told a news conference that the firm would begin filling the pipeline, linking Murzuk with an existing pipeline to the port of Zawiya, in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>Initially it would pump 45,000 barrels of crude a day, rising to its full capacity of 100,000 barrels by the end of 1997, Schenz added.</p>
<p>OMV is developing the Murzuk oilfield with France's Total SA and Spain's Repsol SA.</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom +43 1 53112 258</p>
</text>
